    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d408">

                <pb facs="0780" n="652" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg652"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.2325/15c: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Collier</hi>)<anchor n="31" xml:id="d408-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-07-13T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 13, 1928—2
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>47. Please present my compliments to the President and Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs and express to them the gratification I feel. I am sure their action
                    will be for the best interest of Chile and be considered by all the world as a
                    high-minded and honorable step.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d408-f1" n="31" type="source" xml:id="d408-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, on the same date to the
                    Ambassador in Peru, as telegram No. 57.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
